# Gradle / CI parity (mandatory for agents)

Validate Android changes with the **same commands GitHub Actions runs**. Do not treat “Build succeeded in Android Studio” as a substitute for the CI gate.

## Required commands (repo root)

| Goal | Command | CI workflow |
|------|---------|-------------|
| Unit tests + coverage gate | `./gradlew check` | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` |
| Debug assemble | `./gradlew assembleDebug` | part of always-buildable check |
| UI instrumentation | `./gradlew connectedDebugAndroidTest` (or CI-documented task) | CI UI job when present |
| Release AAB (signed) | documented Play lane / Gradle task | `deploy-play.yml` |

Run from **`knowledge-base-app-android/`** root.

## Before push to `main`

1. **`./gradlew check`** — must pass; enforces **≥ 80%** line coverage.
2. If you changed CI workflows or coverage config, re-read them so local flags match.

## Do NOT use for CI parity

- Only compiling a single module in the IDE
- Skipping JaCoCo “because tests passed”
- Ad-hoc `gradle` flags that differ from `ci.yml`

## Allowed outside the gate

- Quick IDE Run for UX feel on emulator/device
- Editing `VERSION` / docs without a full release upload locally

